From 7d1605f4458892a6746a356011e9d71d1a5d90b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max schwenk <maschwenk@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 03:11:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Find unmatched properties of a lazy target without
 instantiating its members

getUnmatchedPropertiesWorker resolved a target with a lazy member table in
full and looked up every required property in the source with
getPropertyOfType, which instantiates lazy members, although only the
existence of a source property matters without discriminant matching.
This is the relater's path for failing comparisons, where those members
are dropped right after.

With a lazy target, getPropertiesOfTypeLazily lists the properties
getPropertiesOfType would return, in the same order, with declared
members standing in for instantiations the table hasn't created yet (same
names, flags and declarations). It builds the list the way
resolveLazyMembers builds the member table and keeps it on the table, so
base types share it. Without discriminant matching the source is only
asked hasPropertyOfType, which doesn't instantiate lazy members, and the
real target property is looked up only where it's returned or its type
is compared.

38k-file program (37,942 files), tsgo on main + #64475 + #64526 + the
previous commits, median of 3, single threaded / 4 checkers: symbols
13,082,184 -> 12,810,418 (-2.1%) / 19,241,821 -> 18,691,689 (-2.9%),
types and instantiations unchanged, heap after check 10.41 -> 10.37 GB
(-0.4%) / 15.32 -> 15.22 GB (-0.7%), allocations +0.25M (+0.17%) / +0.5M
(+0.2%) for the property lists.

Prototype in a Rust port of the checker (same counts as this commit):
-245K symbols single threaded (-1.8%), -428K with 4 checkers (-2.5%),
measured on the tuple commit alone; before, lazy targets were resolved in
full 34K times (453K symbols) and source lookups instantiated 652K
members, 61% never typed; after, 621,288 / 1,140,871 existence-only
lookups, 152,771 / 340,444 answered by an uninstantiated member; 190,623 /
300,502 property lists requested (including recursive and cached).

lazyMembersUnmatchedProperties.ts covers missing property lists across
declared and inherited members (and their order), the "and N more" form,
private members, implements, and discriminated unions in assignments and
inference. Baselines are generated on main without #64475 and #64526.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
